    "pixelHashCaveat": "pixelHash is the existing noncryptographic 32-bit framebuffer digest plus lit-pixel count; full pixel arrays were not retained."
  },
  "limitations": [
    "OS physical-footprint maximum is a non-atomic sum sampled over the complete observed command family; it is not an exact simultaneous peak and may miss short-lived peaks.",
    "The observed browser command includes startup, installation, server/browser launch, all workload phases, and teardown; these are not isolated renderer-memory measurements.",
    "Observer process-table scanning, browser delivery response hashing, and report generation contribute overhead.",
    "Synchronous CPU timings are diagnostic only and excluded from acceptance because this observer perturbs runtime.",
    "The delivery proof covers recorded requests and confirms the installed entry files and shaper Wasm; it does not claim to authenticate every possible transitive module."
